        <note type="editorial">Liebermann’s <hi rend="italic">genga</hi> is the word element <ref target="entry:genga">-genga</ref> (‘goer’), which occurs only in compounds: <hi rend="italic">æftergenga</hi>, <hi rend="italic">foregenga</hi> (entered as <hi rend="italic">foregengan</hi>) and <hi rend="italic">huslgenga</hi>. It is not <hi rend="italic">gang</hi> (‘going, course’), which has an entry of its own.</note>
